    "title": "DC Forecast | Nice night Saturday, Easter Sunday rain",
    "text": "We've issued a Weather Impact Alert for rain & showers Easter Sunday. WASHINGTON — Three Things to Know: Comfortable Saturday night, 70sSoggy Easter SundayCooler next week Forecast: Saturday Night: Partly cloudy, breezy and warm. Lows: 60s. Winds: SSW 10 - 15.Sunday: Rain and showers ending. Breezy and cooler. Late day clearing. Highs: 67 - 72 (falling throughout the day). Winds: SW/NW 10 - 20.Sunday Night: Cooling down, clearing. Breezy. Lows 35-45. Winds: NW 15. Weather Conversation: With a high of 87 degrees at Dulles this afternoon, a new high temperature record has been broken. The warm, sunny day was such a delight. Hopefully you were able to get in some pre-Easter fun, because the forecast will change over to rain tomorrow. The WUSA9 Weather Team has issued a Weather Impact Alert from 6 a.m. to 6 p.m. as a cold front will pass through, bringing showers, rain, and a few thunderstorms for portions of the day. Early morning church services ahead of 10 a.m. will be fine to get to, but rain and a few rumbles of thunder approach the metro ahead of noon. Spots west of DC, like Frederick and Hagerstown will see showers as early as 9 a.m. The rain will pass slowly, leaving DC wet for a good portion of the afternoon. Around 3-4 p.m. skies will brighten up around the metro, as rain moves east across the Eastern Shore. After the rain we move back to cooler conditions for a stretch of days. Wake up weather Monday will be cool, with morning lows in the 30s and 40s. Expect chilly mornings through the first half of the week. Highs Monday through Wednesday will range through the 50s and lower 60s. Despite the cool down, the week ahead is trending dry, with consistent sunshine. Behind the cold front, temperatures turn cooler for early next week. By Tuesday and Wednesday morning low temperatures will be in the 30s with highs only in the 50s. It won't stay chilly for long, warmer weather returns by the end of the week. 7 DAY FORECAST 10 DAY TEMP TREND ALLERGY INDEX"